      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "To determine whether propranolol can be administered twice daily without any loss of antianginal effect, we studied nine men receiving long-term propranolol therapy for stable angina pectoris. Each patient performed bicycle exercise to the point of angina on two consecutive mornings. By means of double-blind placebo-propranolol administration before the test, the study created a situation whereby on one day the exercise took place 12 hours after the last dose of propranolol, and on the other day 1 1/2 hours after a dose. Despite markedly lower blood levels of propranolol on the day that exercise was performed 12 hours after the last dose, exercise time to angina was nearly identical on the 2 days. We conclude that long-term therapy with propranolol for angina pectoris can be administered on a twice daily basis with no loss of effectiveness."},
